/-!
# The highest-weight normal crystal `B(λ)` of Lakshmibai–Seshadri paths

For a finite reduced root datum `P : RootDatum ι X Y` with a base `b : P.Base` and a dominant
weight `λ ∈ dominantChamber P b`, this file equips `LSPath P b λ` with its canonical parameter-free
normal crystal structure `TauCeti.LSPath.normalCrystal` and identifies it with the connected
component `B(λ)` generated by the dominant straight path `PLPath.straight 𝕜 (f λ)` in any faithful
simple-coroot realization `(f, F)` over a linearly ordered field `𝕜`.

First, in any realization `f : X →+ V` equipped with linear forms `F : b.support → Dual 𝕜 V`
agreeing with the simple coroots on `f(X)` (even without assuming `f` injective on all of `X`), the
image `Set.range (fun π : LSPath P b λ ↦ π.toPLPath 𝕜 f)` is crystal-admissible
(`TauCeti.LSPath.isCrystalSet_range_toPLPath`), combining lattice-valued endpoints
(`TauCeti.LSPath.exists_mem_rootSpan_endpoint_eq_add`), simple-coroot minimum-height integrality
(`TauCeti.LSPath.exists_minHeight_eq_intCast`), and stability under Littelmann's raising and
lowering operators (`TauCeti.LSPath.exists_toPLPath_eq_of_raise_eq_some`,
`TauCeti.LSPath.exists_toPLPath_eq_of_lower_eq_some`). Consequently every realized LS path of
dominant shape — in particular `PLPath.straight 𝕜 (f λ)` — is an integral path in Littelmann's sense
(`TauCeti.LSPath.isIntegralPath_toPLPath`,
`TauCeti.PLPath.isIntegralPath_straight_of_mem_dominantChamber`).

Applying `TauCeti.PLPath.normalCrystalOn` to the canonical rational realization `X →+ ℚ ⊗[ℤ] X` and
transporting along `TauCeti.LSPath.toPLPath_injective_of_coroot'` defines the realization-free
normal crystal `TauCeti.LSPath.normalCrystal` on `LSPath P b λ`. Its weights, raising and lowering
operators, and string lengths are compatible with *every* ordered-field realization `(𝕜, V, f, F)`.
Uniqueness of the highest LS path (`TauCeti.LSPath.forall_raise_eq_none_iff`) together with
finiteness (`TauCeti.LSPath.finite`) implies that `straight λ` is the unique highest element, every
LS path is obtained from `straight λ` by a word of lowering operators
(`TauCeti.LSPath.exists_fWord_straight_eq_some`), and the realized LS paths of shape `λ` are
precisely the paths generated from `PLPath.straight 𝕜 (f λ)` by lowering words or mixed root steps
(`TauCeti.LSPath.range_toPLPath_eq_setOf_exists_lowerWord_straight`,
`TauCeti.LSPath.range_toPLPath_eq_setOf_reflTransGen_rootStep_straight`). When `f` is injective,
this yields the strict crystal isomorphism `TauCeti.LSPath.normalCrystalComponentIso` between the
`a`-chain encoding `LSPath P b λ` and the straight-path component
`PLPath.normalCrystalComponent hf hF ⟨PLPath.straight 𝕜 (f λ), _⟩`. The construction covers `λ = 0`,
chamber walls, nontrivial central characters, and empty root systems uniformly.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.LSPath.normalCrystal`: the canonical normal crystal structure on `LSPath P b λ` for
  `λ ∈ dominantChamber P b`.
* `TauCeti.LSPath.toPLPathCrystalIso`, `TauCeti.LSPath.toPLPathCrystalHom`: strict crystal
  isomorphism with `PLPath.normalCrystalOn` on the realized LS paths and strict embedding into
  `PLPath.normalCrystal`.
* `TauCeti.LSPath.normalCrystalComponentIso`: strict crystal isomorphism between
  `LSPath.normalCrystal` and the connected component `B(λ)` of `PLPath.straight 𝕜 (f λ)` in
  `PLPath.normalCrystal`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.LSPath.isCrystalSet_range_toPLPath`, `TauCeti.LSPath.isIntegralPath_toPLPath`,
  `TauCeti.PLPath.isIntegralPath_straight_of_mem_dominantChamber`: crystal-admissibility and
  integrality of realized LS paths of dominant shape.
* `TauCeti.LSPath.forall_normalCrystal_e_eq_none_iff`,
  `TauCeti.LSPath.exists_fWord_straight_eq_some`,
  `TauCeti.LSPath.connected_normalCrystal_graph`: `straight λ` is the unique highest element and
  generates `LSPath P b λ` under lowering words.
* `TauCeti.LSPath.range_toPLPath_eq_setOf_exists_lowerWord_straight`,
  `TauCeti.LSPath.mem_supp_connectedComponentMk_straight_iff`: equivalence of the `a`-chain LS
  encoding with the operator-generated component of `PLPath.straight 𝕜 (f λ)`.
* `TauCeti.LSPath.eq_straight_of_forall_coroot_eq_zero`,
  `TauCeti.LSPath.eq_straight_of_isEmpty`: singleton crystal structure for `λ = 0`, pure central
  shapes, and empty root systems.

## References

* P. Littelmann, *A Littlewood–Richardson rule for symmetrizable Kac–Moody algebras*, Invent. Math.
  116 (1994), 329–346, §4.
* P. Littelmann, *Paths and root operators in representation theory*, Ann. of Math. 142 (1995),
  499–525, §§2, 4.
* M. Kashiwara, *On crystal bases*, CMS Conf. Proc. 16 (1995), §7.
-/

